{
  "_note": "ALL NUMBERS PLACEHOLDER — straight from pressure-model-illumination.md §4.3, which flags them as guesses. This is the Illumination pattern worked in full; the other seven targets are added by extending this file, not by touching code. A source names its own contributions, and every contribution beyond the one you bind is an IMPLICIT SECONDARY that happens whether you asked for it or not — 'you cannot have bright without hot unless you do something about it'. 'character' is per-target and decides HOW a source contributes: illumination's cyclic sources lift only the peak, constant ones lift peak and floor, occluding ones push both down. 'attachesTo' is the ONE target a source may be bound to. The rune spec §5 says 'each attaches to a target' but never says which — so these follow the spec's own grouping (Celestial, Water, Fire & Thermal, Stone & Mineral, Air, Living, Strange), because a thing attaches to the target it IS an instance of, not to whichever dial it happens to move furthest. Rain can't illuminate. Everything a source does beyond its target still happens as an implicit secondary — you just can't WRITE it. PLACEHOLDER; the palette and the grammar both follow this field. 'attachesTo' is a LIST of the targets a source may be bound to — everything else it does still happens as an implicit secondary. It is a list because some causes belong to more than one target: a volcano is heat and a mountain, a glacier is water and a valley. PLACEHOLDER: Relief currently borrows six sources this way and has no words of its own (volcano, glacier, granite, rift, sand, canopy). Whether it should get its own source runes — mountain, canyon, plain, dune, terrace — is Aimee's call, not mine to invent. SECOND LIGHT IS CUT and RIFT IS FOLDED INTO VOID (Aimee, 6 Aug). Second Light was a nameless extra sun and Count now says 'a pair of suns' better. Rift and Void both meant 'hole in reality' and did opposite things; Void keeps the identity it always had — no sun ever rose here. Rift's arrhythmic Cycle contribution needs rehoming when Cycle gets primaries of its own (cycle-sources-draft.md). THE MOON LIFTS THE NIGHT FLOOR: floor 0 made it a dim sun, and 'the moon is the counter-cyclic light' has to be true in the data. 7 Aug: THE MOON'S NIGHT FLOOR was 4, and Tuning.Pressure.trueDarkFloor is 5 — so writing a moon left the night *below the threshold the game calls pitch dark*. It lifted the night by four points and changed nothing about it, which is the opposite of what its name promises. Now 14: clear of true dark, so a moonlit night is a night you can work in, and a moon-only world reads as constantly dim rather than as a world with no day. PLACEHOLDER.",
